Package: SpectriPyWorkshop
Title: Criss-crossing R and Python for Powerful MS Data Analysis Workflows
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R:
     person(given = "Johannes", family = "Rainer",
            email = "Johannes.Rainer@eurac.edu",
            role = c("aut", "cre"),
            comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6977-7147")
            )
Description:
    This workshop explains how R and Python can be combined in a single
    interactive workflow through the SpectriPy package. The SpectriPy package
    takes care of translating the MS data structures from the two programming
    languages enabling the use of the functions from both in their respective
    native environments.
